JAVA METHOD
- a collection of instructions that perform a specific task
- Main method -> starting programs of execution
- block of code or collection of statement grouped together
- like machines that take input data, process it, and produce output

Parameter
- variable defined in a method declaration

Arguments
- values to be passed inside the parameter
-> input data

Use static when no objects is created

User-defined Method
- method written by the user or programmer
- methods are modified according to the requirement

Pre-defined Method
- method that is already built, that a user can already use

INSTANCES
1. STATIC METHOD
- a method that belongs...
- we can call it without creating an object
- can access static data members and also change the value of it
2. INSTANCE METHOD
- a method that only belong to the object
- can only be called by the object


JAVA SCOPE
1. CLASS SCOPE
2. METHOD SCOPE or LOCAL SCOPE
3. BLOCK SCOPE
4. LOOP SCOPE

